.TH WLANLOGIN 1 2026-11-28 wlanlogin "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
wlanlogin \- automatic login for the Student_CX campus Wi\-Fi portal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlanlogin
.RB [ \-\-user | \-\-system ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B wlanlogin
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wlanlogin
signs in to the Student_CX captive portal and keeps the session online.
Authentication runs only while connected to the Student_CX Wi\-Fi network;
on other networks, credentials can still be saved in advance.
.PP
.B service install
copies the signed
.I wlanlogin.app
bundle into Application Support and registers a LaunchAgent or LaunchDaemon
through SMAppService (macOS 13.0 or later).
The background service monitors Wi\-Fi changes through CoreWLAN and Location
Services, signs in automatically and checks the session periodically.
Every command accepts
.BR \-\-help .
.SH SCOPES
Services, configuration and credentials are kept separately for two scopes.
The scope options may appear before or after the command.
Uninstall the service of one scope before switching to the other.
.TP
.B \-\-user
The current user.
Registers a LaunchAgent that starts at login and stores credentials in the
login keychain (service
.IR dev.cxcs.tools.wlanlogin ,
account
.IR saved\-login ).
Default for non\-root users.
.TP
.B \-\-system
System\-wide.
Registers a LaunchDaemon that starts at boot and stores credentials in the
system keychain (service
.IR dev.cxcs.tools.wlanlogin.system ,
account
.IR saved\-login ).
Requires root privileges and is the default when run as root, for example
through
.BR sudo (8).
Reading the Wi\-Fi SSID still relies on Location Services authorization in an
active desktop session.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR login " [\fIcredential options\fR]"
Sign in with the saved credentials.
Opens a terminal form when credentials are missing.
When not connected to Student_CX, credentials are saved without
authenticating.
A manual login resumes automatic login paused by
.BR logout .
.TP
.BR logout " [" \-\-forget ]
Sign out of the current session and pause automatic login for the current
connection, even across service restarts.
Automatic login resumes after a manual
.B login
in the same scope or after reconnecting to the Wi\-Fi network.
.B \-\-forget
also stops the background service and deletes the saved credentials of the
scope, even when offline or when the portal request fails.
.TP
.BR "service install" " [\fIcredential options\fR]"
Save credentials (required on first installation), copy the signed
.I wlanlogin.app
bundle as the background installation, authorize Keychain and Location
access, then register and start the service through SMAppService.
Run it again after upgrading and re\-signing
.I wlanlogin.app
to update the background copy.
.TP
.BR "service uninstall" " [" \-\-purge ]
Stop and unregister the service and remove the background bundle copy,
keeping saved credentials.
.B \-\-purge
also removes logs, configuration, runtime files and credentials of the
scope.
Location Services permission is managed by macOS and is not reset.
.TP
.BR "service start" ", " "service stop" ", " "service restart"
Start, stop or restart the installed service.
.B stop
keeps the installation and automatic start enabled.
.TP
.B service status
Show whether the service is installed, registered and running, and which
version is installed.
.TP
.BR "service logs" " [" \-n | \-\-lines " \fIlines\fR] [" \-f | \-\-follow ]
Show the service log.
.B \-n
sets the number of recent lines (default 100; 0 shows no history);
.B \-f
follows new entries until interrupted with Ctrl+C.
.TP
.BR "config get " "\fIname\fR, " "config set " "\fIname value\fR"
Read or save a configuration value of the scope.
.TP
.BR "config remove " "\fIname\fR, " "config list"
Restore the default value, or list all values.
The only key is
.BR log.level :
.B info
(default) logs failed portal requests;
.B debug
logs every portal request and response with credentials, cookies and device
identifiers redacted.
Restart the service to apply the change.
.TP
.BR "permission list" ", " "permission check " "[\fIid\fR], " "permission get " \fIid\fR
List, check or request macOS permissions; each accepts
.BR \-\-json .
Available IDs are
.B macos.location
(Location Services for reading the Wi\-Fi SSID) and
.B macos.keychain
(Keychain access for the selected scope).
.B check
queries status without prompting;
.B get
requests the permission in an interactive terminal.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the automatic login loop in the foreground of the current process.
.SH CREDENTIAL OPTIONS
Accepted by
.B login
and
.BR "service install" .
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-username " \fIusername\fR"
Campus network account.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-password " \fIpassword\fR"
Password.
Visible in the process list and shell history; prefer
.BR \-\-password\-stdin .
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
Read one line from standard input as the password.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-p .
.TP
.BR \-\-line " " free1 | free2 | campus
Portal line: free line 1, free line 2, or campus intranet.
.TP
.B \-\-remember\-me
Save the account and password in the keychain of the scope
.RB ( "service install"
always saves credentials).
.TP
.B \-\-interactive
Open the terminal form even when credentials are saved, to change the
account, password or line.
.TP
.B \-\-non\-interactive
Fail instead of opening the terminal form when information is missing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WLANLOGIN_USERNAME
Default for
.BR \-\-username .
.TP
.B WLANLOGIN_PASSWORD
Default for
.BR \-\-password .
.TP
.B WLANLOGIN_LINE
Default for
.BR \-\-line .
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Overrides the log filter of a foreground run, for example
.BR RUST_LOG=wlanlogin::portal::page_config=debug .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/
User scope configuration
.RI ( config.json ),
line preference
.RI ( preferences.json ),
service log
.RI ( daemon.log )
and runtime files.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/wlanlogin.app
User scope background application bundle.
.TP
.I /Library/Application Support/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/state/
System scope configuration, line preference and service log.
.TP
.I /Library/Application Support/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/wlanlogin.app
System scope background application bundle.
.TP
.I /var/run/SEUCXCS/wlanlogin/
System scope runtime files.
.TP
.I dev.cxcs.tools.wlanlogin
Launchd job label in both scopes (embedded as
.IR dev.cxcs.tools.wlanlogin.plist ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed; the reason is printed on standard error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install the user service and check it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wlanlogin \-\-user service install
wlanlogin \-\-user service status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check or request macOS permissions:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wlanlogin \-\-user permission check
wlanlogin \-\-user permission get macos.location
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sign in from a script without exposing the password:
.PP
.RS
.EX
printf \(aq%s\en\(aq "$PASSWORD" | wlanlogin login \-u 2026000000 \e
    \-\-password\-stdin \-\-line free1 \-\-non\-interactive
.EE
.RE
.PP
Switch account or line:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wlanlogin logout
wlanlogin login \-\-interactive \-\-remember\-me
.EE
.RE
.PP
Collect portal diagnostics:
.PP
.RS
.EX
wlanlogin \-\-user config set log.level debug
wlanlogin \-\-user service restart
wlanlogin \-\-user service logs \-f
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Requires macOS 13.0 or later and a signed
.I wlanlogin.app
bundle.
Do not modify files inside the bundle after signing, and reuse the same
signing identity when upgrading so Location Services and Keychain approvals
carry over.
.PP
If background activity requires approval after
.BR "service install" ,
enable CXCS WLAN Login under System Settings \(-> General \(-> Login Items,
then run
.BR "wlanlogin \-\-user service start" .
.PP
Apple requires notarization for native LaunchDaemons, so locally
self\-signed bundles may be rejected in
.B \-\-system
scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR launchctl (1),
.BR codesign (1),
.BR security (1)
.PP
https://github.com/SEUCXCS/wlan\-auto\-login
